From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: 8723b: always report a single spatial stream

Carried from the upstream rtw-next commit

  b490cf696ff715abf5c84f69b02b989ea49052d2
  "wifi: rtw88: 8723b: always report a single spatial stream"
  (Luka Gejak, 2026-10-20)

which is *not* part of the upstream snapshot this module is built from
(05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d, a torvalds/linux master
snapshot of 2026-11-03): master only merged rtw-next up to the
"rtw-next-2026-10-08" tag, so every 8723B fix from 2026-10-09 onwards
is missing from the tree we ship.

Why we carry it:

  The RTL8723B only ever has one spatial stream.  The shipped tree
  derives nss from rtwdev->hal.rf_path_num and only clamps it to a
  minimum of one, so the reported capability depends on how far the RF
  path setup has progressed when the efuse is read.

  Setting nss and ant_num to one directly is what upstream does, and it
  removes a dependency on the RF path being initialised before the
  capability is reported.
---
diff --git a/rtw8723b.c b/rtw8723b.c
index f2164a7333e6..19bb9fd7417b 100644
--- a/rtw8723b.c
+++ b/rtw8723b.c
@@ -2397,12 +2397,9 @@ static int rtw8723b_read_efuse(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, u8 *log_map, u8 *phy_map)
 	if (efuse->power_track_type != 0)
 		rtw_warn(rtwdev, "unsupported power track type\n");
 
-	/*
-	 * No firmware hardware feature report exists, so fill the hardware
-	 * capability here; a zero stream count kills the HT MCS set.
-	 */
-	efuse->hw_cap.nss = max_t(u8, rtwdev->hal.rf_path_num, 1);
-	efuse->hw_cap.ant_num = efuse->hw_cap.nss;
+	/* No firmware hardware feature report exists, so fill it in here. */
+	efuse->hw_cap.nss = 1;
+	efuse->hw_cap.ant_num = 1;
 	efuse->hw_cap.bw = BIT(RTW_CHANNEL_WIDTH_20) |
 			   BIT(RTW_CHANNEL_WIDTH_40);
 
